 `algorithm/geometry_resolver.slangh` use it. Diffuse and glossy gathers use the ordinary disk-free sky.
 `pass/numos/numos_disc.h` holds the rim and peak equations also checked by `test_enhanced_sky.cpp`.
 The emitted lights and the standalone library shaders keep their physical illuminance.
+
+## The Night sky editor on the Enhanced camera sky and mirrors
+
+- `rtx_fork_numos_night.*` assembles the editor controls, eclipse overlap and twilight weights.
+  `rtx_atmosphere.*` shares its four cached DDS views and load-by-path logic, including missing-layer
+  stand-ins. `rtx_numos.*` registers the source choice, prepares the night uniforms before the G-buffer
+  and binds the PSR and composite resources. The catalogue checkbox in `rtx_numos_ui.cpp` edits
+  the same source. `src/dxvk/meson.build` includes the new host source.
+- `rtx_numos_gpu.*` identifies the sky-view pass and its bound constants before restoring the stellar
+  part of in-scatter that the catalogue switch removed. All 41 library programs use their pin.
+- `pass/numos/numos_night.h` and `numos_night.slangh` hold the calibrated image, meteors, lunar glow
+  and solar corona. `numos_visible_discs.slangh`, the composite bindings and the PSR miss in
+  `algorithm/geometry_resolver.slangh` compose them behind air, lunar coverage and clouds.
+  `test_enhanced_sky.cpp` checks calibration, twilight, totality, star-air flags and block layout.
