+### The Enhanced night
+
+The camera composite and the primary-surface-replacement miss use the same celestial frame, lunar mask
+and night radiance. With `rtx.atmosphere.numos.nightSkyImage` on, the four NightSky HD DDS layers
+use the Night sky editor's weights, colours and master brightness. Choosing the physical catalogue
+restores the library's ordinary visible night. Shooting stars and the Moon's Gaussian glow work with
+either source. A solar occultation adds the chromosphere and corona around the existing disc.
+
+The 80-byte `NumosNightArgs` slice is ready before the G-buffer. The camera binds it at 97, its four DDS
+views at 98–101 and its wrap-U sampler at 102. The PSR miss uses 414 and the existing night-image
+slots. The two modes share the texture cache, including zero-weight release and tier-specific filenames.
+
+NUMOS couples the catalogue to both blurred direct starlight in the sky LUT and 40 S10 of stellar
+illumination scattered by the air. Image mode clears its effective catalogue setting before the LUT
+bake. The DXVK adapter restores the missing scattered light to the sky-view pass with the current
+stellar gain and pre-exposed reference illuminance. The physical airglow, zodiacal light and lunar
+lighting keep their library settings. The full-sphere Milky Way calibration uses the two shipped
+assets before atmospheric extinction, exposure or tone mapping.
+
 ### Lights
 
 The sun, moons and lightning are externally tracked lights, one frame behind the renderer. Distant lights with `lightFlagCloudShadowed` get the cloud shadow in direct and indirect next event estimation, and in the volume integration. Resampling ignores the shadow.
